. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["ONE Gas, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $5.1B market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 57% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $128M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.2\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 1.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Price sits 23% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2264527372809334},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Utilities peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Growing faster than most Utilities peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ONE Gas (NYSE:OGS) Announces Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/one-gas-nyseogs-announces-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793945083.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"ONE Gas (OGS) Stock Could Be Fully Priced Following Raised 2026 Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-ogs/one-gas/news/one-gas-ogs-stock-could-be-fully-priced-following-raised-202","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793885684.917,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.913,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"ONE Gas (NYSE:OGS) Posts Quarterly Earnings Results, Beats Expectations By $0.05 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/one-gas-nyseogs-posts-quarterly-earnings-results-beats-expectations-by-0-05-eps.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestam